;; FH-CALL-004 — the crossing is invisible in the output.
;;
;; Four declarations, one body, every pairing of parent mode and child
;; mode. All four render the SAME tree once the two ids that name WHICH
;; declaration ran are erased — `:fh/parent` for the parent's own view
;; id, `:fh/child` for the child's. Those two are the only substitutions
;; the suite is allowed, and they are not a mode difference at all: a view
;; id names the declaration a view IS, and four pairings need four
;; declarations.
;;
;; The 2 x 2 is the point. Two cases alone would prove that two things
;; agree; the matrix proves that neither axis is visible, and it includes
;; the no-crossing control (compiled parent, compiled child) so the
;; agreement is measured against something rather than only against
;; itself.
{:fh/id "FH-CALL-004"
 :fh/law
 "An interpreted parent mounts a compiled descriptor and a compiled parent mounts a statically named interpreted descriptor, both through the ordinary named-descriptor boundary; all four mode pairings of one body yield one structural tree."

 ;; The boundary call every case is mounted with.
 :args {:items [1 2]}

 :cases
 [{:note "neither side compiled — the baseline the other three are held to"
   :view :interpreted-parent-interpreted-child
   :parent-lowering :interpreted
   :child-lowering  :interpreted
   :child-view-id   :re-frame.freehand.tree-views/row}

  {:note "an interpreted parent mounts a COMPILED descriptor"
   :view :interpreted-parent-compiled-child
   :parent-lowering :interpreted
   :child-lowering  :compiled
   :child-view-id   :re-frame.freehand.compiled-views/row}

  {:note "a compiled parent mounts a statically named INTERPRETED descriptor"
   :view :compiled-parent-interpreted-child
   :parent-lowering :compiled
   :child-lowering  :interpreted
   :child-view-id   :re-frame.freehand.tree-views/row}

  {:note "both sides compiled — the control, where nothing crosses"
   :view :compiled-parent-compiled-child
   :parent-lowering :compiled
   :child-lowering  :compiled
   :child-view-id   :re-frame.freehand.compiled-views/row}]

 ;; The one tree, in placeholder ids. Each case's parent id becomes
 ;; `:fh/parent` and its child id `:fh/child` before the comparison.
 :tree
 {:view-id  :fh/parent
  :props    {:items [1 2]}
  :children [{:tag   :ul
              :attrs {:class "rows"}
              :children
              [{:view-id  :fh/child
                :props    {:label 1}
                :key      1
                :children [{:tag :li :attrs {:class "row"} :children ["1"]}]}
               {:view-id  :fh/child
                :props    {:label 2}
                :key      2
                :children [{:tag :li :attrs {:class "row"} :children ["2"]}]}]}]
  :rf.ui/tree-version 1}}
